update public.journey_milestones
set summary = $su$September and October took the AI First journey into campus operations. Using the Zoho Creator low-code platform, HKBK began building its own digital systems for Hostel Management and Attendance Management, replacing manual registers and spreadsheets with secure, role-based apps and live dashboards. Alongside this, a new Alumni Portal is being developed as part of the HKBK college website. The systems are being built in-house by HKBK students under faculty mentorship.$su$,
    points = array[
    $p0$Hostel Management System for the Boys and Girls hostels: one central app with role-based access for the Principal, Super Admin, Wardens, Operations and Students$p0$,
    $p1$Live hostel dashboards with student search, fee tracking, attendance calendar, memos and quick actions$p1$,
    $p2$Automated account approvals, maintenance and service tickets raised by students and handled by the Operations team, with urgent-ticket flagging by the Principal$p2$,
    $p3$Branded printable reports with one-click PDF and CSV download, carrying the HKBK logo, college name and timestamps$p3$,
    $p4$Attendance Management system to record and track attendance digitally, with summaries for faculty and administrators$p4$,
    $p5$Secure by design: each user sees only the data their role allows$p5$,
    $p6$Alumni Portal on the HKBK college website to build the alumni network: alumni registration, profiles and a channel to stay connected with the college$p6$
    ]::text[],
    layer = 4
where slug = 'm-2026-10';

-- ============================================================
-- Content
-- ============================================================
insert into public.pages (slug, title, summary, body_md) values
  ('about', 'About HKBK College of Engineering', 'An engineering college in Nagawara, Bengaluru, affiliated to VTU and approved by AICTE, teaching engineers since 1997.', '## Who we are

HKBK College of Engineering was founded in 1997 as part of the HKBK Group of Institutions. The college is affiliated to Visvesvaraya Technological University (VTU), Belagavi, and approved by the All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE), New Delhi.

The campus is in Nagawara, north Bengaluru, directly opposite Manyata Tech Park, one of the city''s largest technology business parks. That location shapes how we teach: industry engineers visit as guest faculty, students take internships across the road, and our consultancy and training teams work with companies next door.

We offer the Bachelor of Engineering in five branches (Computer Science, Information Science, Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning, Mechanical, and Electronics & Communication) and doctoral research through six research centres.

The college has committed to becoming an AI First and Quantum Ready campus. Read what that means for [students and staff](/ai-quantum/ai-first), how the [Quantum Lab](/ai-quantum/quantum-lab) works, and follow progress on our [dashboards](/ai-quantum/dashboards).'),
  ('academics', 'Departments', 'Five engineering departments, the basic sciences and humanities, and physical education and sports.', 'Every department teaches the VTU curriculum and adds AI to it: students learn to use AI tools in their discipline, and to judge when not to. Select a department to read its vision and mission.'),
  ('ai-champions', 'AI Champions and Ambassadors', 'Fifteen AI Faculty Champions and fifty AI Student Ambassadors lead HKBK''s move to an AI First campus.', ''),
  ('ai-first', 'AI First campus', 'AI where it genuinely helps students and staff, with clear rules about privacy, fairness and human judgement.', '## What students get

- **Campus assistant.** Answers questions about courses, timetables, fees, policies and events from official college documents. It shows its sources and says "I don''t know" rather than guessing.
- **Study tutor.** Explains concepts and quizzes students on their own courses. It guides students to answers rather than handing over graded work. Faculty decide how it is used in each course.
- **AI in every programme.** Every branch uses AI tools in its labs and projects, from code assistants in Computer Science to design analysis in Civil and Mechanical Engineering.
- **AI literacy.** Short modules for every student on prompting, checking answers, protecting personal data and recognising bias.

## What faculty and staff get

- **Faculty copilot.** Drafts lesson plans, quizzes and feedback. Faculty review and approve everything before students see it.
- **Office copilot.** Sorts helpdesk requests and drafts summaries and reports, so staff spend less time on paperwork.

## Our rules for AI

1. AI never makes final decisions about admissions, grades or discipline. People do.
2. The assistant only uses information the person asking is allowed to see.
3. Conversations with the assistant are private to the user. Usage reports show totals, never individual chats.
4. AI answers cite their sources.
5. We publish what each AI system can and cannot do, and review them every semester.

## Office of the Chief AI Officer

The Chief AI Officer leads AI strategy, governance and the [dashboards](/ai-quantum/dashboards) that track progress.'),
  ('ai-quantum', 'AI and quantum at HKBK', 'Two commitments for the next decade. Every engineer learns to build with AI, and the campus prepares students and systems for quantum computing.', '**AI First** means AI is part of how every programme is taught and how campus services work, with clear rules for privacy, fairness and human judgement.

**Quantum Ready** has two halves. Students learn quantum computing hands-on, from simulators to real quantum hardware. And the systems that hold student and research records move to the new quantum-safe encryption standards, so that data stolen today cannot be decrypted by quantum computers later.'),
  ('alumni', 'Alumni', 'HKBK Alumni Network — portal coming soon', ''),
  ('consultancy', 'Consultancy projects', 'Faculty-led teams that take on engineering, software and AI problems for industry, government and the community.', '## What we take on

- **AI and software**: prototypes, data analysis, machine learning models and web applications.
- **Electronics and IoT**: embedded prototypes, sensor networks and testing.
- **Civil engineering**: structural assessment, materials testing and design review.
- **Mechanical engineering**: design, analysis and manufacturing support.
- **Management**: market studies and business analytics from our MBA faculty.

## How an engagement works

1. **Tell us the problem** in the [Request consultancy](#enquire) tab.
2. **Scoping call.** A faculty coordinator discusses requirements, data and timelines with you.
3. **Proposal.** You receive the scope, team, timeline and fee in writing.
4. **Delivery.** A faculty-led team, often with student researchers, does the work and reports progress.
5. **Handover.** You receive the results, a report and any code or drawings agreed in the proposal.'),
  ('contact', 'Contact', 'Visit, call or write to HKBK College of Engineering in Nagawara, Bengaluru.', ''),
  ('corporate-training', 'Corporate training', 'Short, practical programmes in AI, quantum computing, software and core engineering for working teams, on our campus or at yours.', '## Why train with HKBK

- **Next door to your office.** The campus is directly opposite Manyata Tech Park.
- **Hands-on.** Every programme is built around labs and exercises with your own use cases where possible.
- **Faculty and practitioners together.** Sessions are led by our faculty with guest experts from industry.
- **Flexible.** Run a programme at our campus, at your office or online, on weekdays or weekends.

Participants who complete a programme receive a certificate from HKBK College of Engineering.'),
  ('dashboards', 'AI and quantum dashboards', 'Live views of how AI and quantum computing are used across the campus. Each dashboard appears here as soon as it is published.', 'Our AI office is building these dashboards in stages. Dashboards marked **In development** are not public yet. When a dashboard goes live, an **Open dashboard** link appears beside it.'),
  ('home-ai-first', 'AI-First Campus', 'Paragraphs shown on the home page under "AI-First Campus".', 'HKBK is building an AI-First campus, where artificial intelligence is part of how every student learns, every teacher teaches and every service runs. Students in all five BE programmes learn to use AI tools in their own discipline, to check what those tools produce, and to build AI systems of their own.

Faculty use AI to design richer courses and give faster, more personal feedback, while clear rules keep people, not algorithms, in charge of grades and other decisions that affect students. Leading the change are our AI Faculty Champions, who guide AI adoption in every department, and our AI Student Ambassadors, who run peer workshops and help classmates use AI responsibly.'),
  ('houses', 'Houses', 'Every HKBK student belongs to one of five houses, which compete and serve together through the year.', 'The house system builds friendship across departments and years. Houses compete in sport, culture, technical events and community service, and earn points for the house cup through the year. Each house has faculty mentors and student captains.'),
  ('ieee', 'IEEE Student Branch', 'The HKBK IEEE Student Branch and its chapters connect students with the world''s largest technical professional organisation.', '## About the branch

The IEEE Student Branch at HKBK College of Engineering brings together students from every engineering department who want to learn beyond the syllabus. Members meet engineers and researchers, build projects, and take part in IEEE events across India. The branch runs chapters for specific IEEE societies and affinity groups, listed in the tabs above.

## CIS

**IEEE Computational Intelligence Society (CIS) chapter.** The IEEE Computational Intelligence Society covers neural networks, fuzzy systems, evolutionary computation and other nature-inspired approaches to artificial intelligence. The HKBK chapter runs talks, coding challenges and project groups in machine learning and AI, in step with our AI First Campus.

## WIE

**IEEE Women in Engineering (WIE) affinity group.** IEEE Women in Engineering works to inspire, support and connect women engineers and scientists. The HKBK WIE group runs mentoring, leadership sessions, outreach to schools and technical workshops that encourage more women to lead in engineering.

## Information Theory

**IEEE Information Theory Society chapter.** The IEEE Information Theory Society deals with how information is processed, transmitted, stored and protected, from coding theory and data compression to communication and cryptography. The HKBK chapter connects students in communications, signal processing and quantum-safe security.

## Education Society

**IEEE Education Society chapter.** The IEEE Education Society focuses on the theory and practice of education in engineering and computing, including educational technology. The HKBK chapter explores new ways of teaching and learning, including how AI can support students and faculty.

## Activities

- **Technical talks** by engineers and researchers from industry and academia.
- **Workshops** on AI, embedded systems, IoT, quantum computing and more.
- **Competitions and hackathons**, including IEEE contests and paper presentations.
- **Industry visits** to companies across Bengaluru.

## Membership

Any HKBK student can join IEEE as a student member and add society memberships such as CIS, Information Theory or Education Society, or join Women in Engineering. Members get access to IEEE publications, technical societies, scholarships and a global professional network. Contact the branch counsellor to join.'),
  ('initiatives', 'Centres and initiatives', 'Dedicated hubs for human values, research, innovation, skills, inclusion and our alumni, each growing into its own HKBK website.', 'Each centre and initiative is run by the cell or office responsible for it, and will open at its own HKBK web address. Until then, each one has a page here with what it does.'),
  ('iqac', 'Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC)', 'The IQAC plans, guides and monitors quality across teaching, research and administration at HKBK.', '## About IQAC

The Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) was set up to make quality a continuous part of college life, in line with the guidelines of the National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC). It works with every department to plan improvements, track progress and share good practice.

## Objectives

- Build a culture of quality in teaching, learning, research and administration.
- Develop clear benchmarks and track performance against them.
- Bring student, parent, alumni and employer feedback into planning.
- Prepare the college for assessment and accreditation.

## Functions

- Collects and analyses feedback from students, faculty, parents, alumni and employers.
- Organises faculty development programmes, workshops and seminars on quality.
- Documents academic and administrative audits and best practices.
- Prepares the Annual Quality Assurance Report (AQAR) and other submissions to NAAC.

## Reports and minutes

AQARs, meeting minutes and the IQAC composition will be published here.'),
  ('mous', 'MoUs', 'Memoranda of Understanding that connect HKBK with industry, universities, research organisations and government bodies.', '## What our MoUs cover

- **Internships and projects** for students with partner companies.
- **Training and certification** in emerging technologies, including AI and quantum computing.
- **Joint research**, publications and funded projects with faculty and research scholars.
- **Guest lectures, workshops and industry visits** that bring practitioners to campus.
- **Placements** and pre-placement talks for final-year students.'),
  ('news', 'News and events', 'What is happening at HKBK, from campus events to new programmes and achievements.', ''),
  ('placements', 'Placements', 'The placement cell prepares HKBK students for careers and connects them with recruiters, from Manyata Tech Park and beyond.', '## How we prepare students

- **Career readiness training** in aptitude, communication, interviews and group discussions, starting in the early semesters.
- **Industry-ready skills** through the Skill Development Centre, certification courses and AI tools in every programme.
- **Internships** with companies, many of them a short walk away at Manyata Tech Park.
- **Mock interviews and resume reviews** with faculty and alumni mentors.

## For recruiters

Companies can schedule campus drives, internships and pre-placement talks with the placement cell. Contact the college to plan a drive.

## Our recruiters

Recruiter logos and placement statistics by year will be added here.'),
  ('programmes', 'Programmes', 'Bachelor of Engineering in five branches, under the VTU curriculum, with AI built into every programme.', 'Each programme is a four-year Bachelor of Engineering (BE) affiliated to Visvesvaraya Technological University (VTU), Belagavi. First-year students study mathematics, physics, chemistry and the humanities alongside the basics of their branch.'),
  ('quantum-lab', 'Quantum Ready Campus', 'In our Quantum Lab students move from circuit simulators to real quantum hardware, while the campus moves its own security to quantum-safe encryption.', '## Learning tracks

- **Foundations.** Qubits, superposition, entanglement, gates and measurement.
- **Algorithms.** Grover''s search, the quantum Fourier transform, and variational algorithms such as VQE and QAOA.
- **Quantum-safe cryptography.** Why quantum computers threaten today''s encryption, and how the new NIST standards (ML-KEM, ML-DSA and SLH-DSA) replace it.
- **Research projects.** Final-year and doctoral projects that use quantum computing in chemistry, optimisation or machine learning.

## A quantum-safe campus

Quantum computers powerful enough to break today''s public-key encryption do not exist yet. But attackers can store encrypted data now and decrypt it later. Student records and research data stay valuable for decades, so HKBK is moving them to quantum-safe protection early:

- Website traffic uses hybrid post-quantum key exchange where browsers support it.
- Sensitive records are encrypted with keys protected by post-quantum algorithms.
- Digital certificates and transcripts will carry post-quantum signatures that anyone can verify.
- All cryptography is tracked in one inventory, so algorithms can be upgraded quickly as standards evolve.'),
  ('research-centres', 'Research centres', 'Six research centres for doctoral research in engineering and the basic sciences.', 'Each centre is led by its department and supports PhD scholars with supervisors, laboratories and computing resources. Contact the centre''s department to discuss research admissions and collaborations.'),
  ('research', 'Research and development', 'Doctoral research, funded projects and faculty-led work in AI, quantum computing and core engineering.', '## Research centre

HKBK has six research centres for doctoral research: Computer Science & Engineering, Electronics & Communication Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Chemistry, Physics and Mathematics. Scholars work with faculty supervisors and have access to the college''s labs, library and computing resources. See all [research centres](/research/centres).

## Focus areas

- **Artificial intelligence and machine learning**: language models, computer vision, AI for education and healthcare.
- **Quantum computing and quantum-safe security**: quantum algorithms, post-quantum cryptography and migration.
- **Electronics**: VLSI, embedded systems, IoT and signal processing.
- **Basic sciences**: materials, photonics, green chemistry, applied mathematics and statistics.
- **Mechanical systems**: design, manufacturing, thermal engineering and robotics.

## Work with us

Companies and research organisations can sponsor projects, co-supervise scholars or share equipment. Start with a [consultancy request](/consultancy#enquire) or [contact the college](/contact).'),
  ('uhv', 'Universal Human Values', 'Our UHV cell helps students and staff think clearly about values, relationships and their place in society, as part of AICTE''s Universal Human Values programme.', '## What UHV is

The All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE) introduced Universal Human Values (UHV) into the student induction programme and the engineering curriculum. UHV asks a simple question: what does it mean to live and work well with others?

Students explore themselves, their families, society and nature through guided self-reflection and discussion, not through lectures on rules. The aim is clarity: understanding what you value, and acting on it.

## How UHV runs at HKBK

- **Induction (UHV-I)** for every first-year student, before regular classes begin.
- **The UHV course (UHV-II)** as part of the curriculum.
- **Faculty development programmes**, so that mentors can facilitate UHV sessions well.
- **Reflection circles and outreach** through the year.

## Why it matters on an AI First campus

Students here learn to build powerful AI systems. They also need judgement about fairness, privacy and the people their work affects. UHV gives that judgement a foundation, and our values-and-technology talks connect it directly to AI and engineering decisions.'),
  ('vision-mission', 'Vision and mission', 'The vision and mission of HKBK College of Engineering.', '## Vision

To be a campus where every engineer learns to build with artificial intelligence, is prepared for quantum technologies, and works with integrity for society.

## Mission

- Teach every programme with AI tools, and teach students to build and question them.
- Give students hands-on access to quantum computing, from simulators to real hardware.
- Grow research and consultancy that solve problems for industry and the community.
- Shape character alongside skill through Universal Human Values.
- Protect the data of our students and staff with modern, quantum-safe security.')
on conflict (slug) do update set title = excluded.title, summary = excluded.summary, body_md = excluded.body_md;
insert into public.leadership_messages (slug, name, designation, organisation, excerpt, photo_url, body_md, sort_order, section) values
  ('chairman', 'Shri. C M Ibrahim', 'Chairman', 'HKBK Group of Institutions', 'We opened HKBK in 1997 to give every young person a fair chance at an excellent engineering education. Becoming an AI First and Quantum Ready campus is how we keep that promise for the next generation.', '/images/leaders/chairman.jpg', 'Dear students, parents and partners,

When HKBK College of Engineering opened its doors in 1997, our aim was simple: to give young people from every background a fair chance at an excellent engineering education. That aim has not changed. What has changed is the world our graduates walk into.

Artificial intelligence is now part of how software is written, how buildings are designed, and how hospitals and factories run. Quantum computing is moving out of research laboratories and into its first real applications. The engineers who lead over the next twenty years will be the ones who understand both, and who use them responsibly.

That is why we have committed HKBK to becoming an AI First and Quantum Ready campus. Every department will teach with AI tools and teach students how to build them. Our Quantum Lab will let students run their own circuits on real quantum hardware. And the systems that hold student and research records will move to the new quantum-safe security standards.

Technology alone does not make a good engineer. Through our Universal Human Values programme, we ask every student to think about the people their work will serve. Skill and character must grow together.

Our campus sits directly opposite Manyata Tech Park, and industry is our neighbour. I invite companies to train their teams with us, to bring us their engineering problems, and to hire our graduates.

To our students: work hard, stay curious, and look after one another. To parents: thank you for trusting us with your children''s future.', 1, 'leadership'),
  ('chief-ai-quantum-officer', 'Dr. Tabassum Ara', 'Chief AI and Quantum Officer', 'Dean IIC and HoD, Dept. of AIML, HKBK College of Engineering', 'Our campus does not just teach AI, we live it.', '/images/leaders/tabassum-ara.jpg', 'Every achievement in this journey — the portals we built, the students we trained, the recognitions we earned — comes from one belief: that AI without humanity is incomplete. We have woven Human Values and Ethics into every AI initiative.

Our intake in AIML has grown from 120 to 180 students — not because we marketed AI, but because we demonstrated AI. I built four live AI applications using Claude — a video library, a prompt library, a health tracker, and a student chatbot — to show that our campus does not just teach AI, we live it. Every sponsorship we earned, every collaboration we secured, began with this proof.

- **AIML Intake:** Expanded from 120 to 180 students due to AI-first brand positioning.
- **AICTE Sponsorship:** Secured funding for AI + Cybersecurity program development.
- **Quantum Computing:** Sponsorship secured from VAANI and ATAL for Quantum readiness.
- **Human Values:** All AI-First programs incorporate ethics, UHV, and responsible AI principles.
- **Industry Training:** HKBK now trains IT professionals in AI — creating new revenue and recognition.', 1, 'ai-first'),
  ('director', 'Shri. C M Faiz Mohammed', 'Director', 'HKBK Group of Institutions', 'AI-First is not a strategy for us; it is a survival imperative and a moral responsibility.', '/images/leaders/director.jpg', 'The IT industry is changing faster than any of us anticipated. When AI automates coding, testing, and system administration, what will happen to our graduates? This question kept me awake. The answer is not to fear AI, but to master it.

We are not just teaching engineering. We are preparing human beings who will collaborate with AI, lead AI teams, and build AI systems. If IT jobs disappear, our students must be the ones who create the next wave of AI-powered opportunities. That is why AI-First is not a strategy for us; it is a survival imperative and a moral responsibility.

- **AI-First Mandate:** Every department, every subject, every semester must integrate AI by 2027.
- **Future-Proofing:** Our students will not compete with AI; they will direct it.
- **Global Positioning:** HKBK will be recognised as India''s AI-First engineering college.', 2, 'leadership'),
  ('principal', 'Dr. Mohammed Riyaz Ahmed', 'Principal', 'HKBK College of Engineering', 'Admissions of the future will be won not by physical infrastructure alone, but by the quality and depth of our academic and AI infrastructure.', '/images/leaders/principal.jpg', 'When parents and students choose an engineering college today, they look at buildings and laboratories. In 2026 and beyond, they will ask: what AI infrastructure does this college have? What AI skills will my child gain? Does this college have access to real AI tools?

We began this year with awareness sessions to break down the fear and confusion around AI. Every department head, every faculty member needed to understand not just what AI is, but how it applies to their discipline. Today, our campus runs on AI-powered portals, AI-assisted teaching, and AI-integrated curriculum. Admissions of the future will be won not by physical infrastructure alone, but by the quality and depth of our academic and AI infrastructure.

- **Academic Infrastructure:** AI tools, portals, and curriculum as competitive differentiators in admissions.
- **Faculty Transformation:** Teachers who use AI in the classroom inspire students to master it.
- **Outcome Focus:** Every AI initiative must improve placement rates, NAAC scores, and student competency.', 3, 'leadership')
on conflict (slug) do update set name = excluded.name, designation = excluded.designation, organisation = excluded.organisation, excerpt = excluded.excerpt, photo_url = excluded.photo_url, body_md = excluded.body_md, sort_order = excluded.sort_order, section = excluded.section;
